## Adapted / inherited source code

### dsh-wsl-workspace (MIT) — https://github.com/6Mikao9/dsh-wsl-workspace

Copyright (c) 6Mikao9 (mimikao).

This plugin is a direct adaptation of `dsh-wsl-workspace`: the host half
(`src/index.ts`, `src/host/variants.ts`), the provider structure
(`src/shell.ts`, `src/fs.ts`), the shared path/store helpers, and the browser
half (`src/client/*`) are derived from that repository, with the WSL execution
world (wsl.exe + 9P UNC filesystem) replaced by a Windows Docker execution
world (docker exec + bind-mount filesystem).

### DeepSeek Harness (MIT) — https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness

Copyright (c) DeepSeek (Beijing) Intelligent Technology Co., Ltd.

This plugin is part of the DeepSeek Harness ecosystem and directly adapts or
inherits source code from the upstream repository:

- `@deepseek-ai/dsh-pwsh-local` (packages/shell/pwsh-local) — the executor
  mechanics of `DockerShellExecutor` (`src/shell.ts`) are adapted from this
  package: the fused timeout/abort deadline, bounded collect output with
  spill files, the background-process adaptation, and the `ENCODING_PREAMBLE`
  UTF-8 output pinning. The `docker exec` argv and workdir planning are
  original to this plugin.
- `@deepseek-ai/dsh-fs-local` (packages/fs/fs-local) — `DockerFileSystem`
  (`src/fs.ts`) subclasses `LocalFileSystem` unchanged for realpath target
  identity, per-target write locks, atomic staging, and version guards, adding
  only the container↔host path translation over the bind mounts.
- `apps/cli/config/agent-presets/{standard,minimal,code,cordis}/agent.cordis.yml`
  — the preset-variant generator (`src/host/variants.ts`) reads and
  transforms these shipped compositions; the variant persona text is
  rewritten from the `standard` persona.

The upstream license text applies to the adapted portions above.

## Design references (no source code copied)

### dsh-remote-ssh (MIT) — https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-remote-ssh

The transparent per-workspace execution-world routing pattern (fs/search/shell
routed to a remote world without a second tool set) informed the architecture
of this plugin. No source files were copied.

## Dependency licenses (runtime, resolved from the hosting harness)

At runtime this plugin imports `@deepseek-ai/cordis`, `@deepseek-ai/dsh-fs`,
`@deepseek-ai/dsh-fs-local`, `@deepseek-ai/dsh-shell`,
`@deepseek-ai/dsh-subprocess`, and `@deepseek-ai/dsh-timeout` as peer
dependencies provided by the DeepSeek Harness installation (MIT). No
